From 325252a4656f727a7a82f9a6cccacf6cb8263599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:26:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 70/70] vgpu: load depth and stencil in later records of one
 render encoder

Component: runtime exec, the multi-draw chain of one Metal render encoder
(all pathways that encode a record as its own Vulkan render pass).

Each record after the first already had its colour load actions forced to
Load, because Metal applies the pass load action once when the encoder
begins. Depth and stencil kept the pass's own action. That meant a Clear ran
again before every record, so a later draw tested against a cleared buffer.

RenderBox on 26 and 27 draws an icon shape with depth writes on, then fills
outside it with a full-target quad behind a GreaterEqual test. With depth
cleared again, that quad passed everywhere and erased the shape, and
iconservicesagent logged "Flattened representation is seemingly a fully
transparent image". The Dock and Spotlight then showed the generic
placeholder for Finder, Messages, Notes, Reminders, Music, App Store,
Terminal and others. The engine already honours a depth Load against a
resident that holds content (registry_mark_depth_ready), so the runtime
only has to ask for it.

The colour loop and the two new cases are one function, load_prior_record,
with a unit test.

Verified:
- cargo test -p reims-vgpu --no-default-features
  --features backend-vulkan,host-window -- --test-threads=1: 2344 lib tests
  (including the new one) and every integration test pass.
- clippy -D warnings: 65 diagnostics with and without this change on rustc
  1.99.1. None of them are new.
- Live on arm64 Linux (NVIDIA GB10), macOS 27.2 guest. I cleared the
  iconservicesagent, iconservices.store and dock.iconcache caches and
  restarted Dock and the icon agents. Every Dock icon then drew correctly,
  and no icon render left an all-zero store. Before the change 8 Dock icons
  were placeholders. About This Mac also drew its text on first open; before,
  the text only appeared after a click.

Not verified: the backend-metal and x86 clippy arms, and other macOS
versions at the time of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
